   "modified": "2026-07-30T19:47:27",
   "modified_gmt": "2026-07-30T19:47:27",
   "slug": "robotic-actuators-company",
   "status": "publish",
   "type": "company",
   "link": "https://hax.co/company/robotic-actuators-company/",
   "title": {
    "rendered": "Robotic Actuators Company"
   },
   "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>RAC (Robotic Actuators Company) is building a scalable mobile robot platform powered by a battery-electric Digital Hydraulic Transmission (DHT) that targets electric-like efficiency with hydraulic-class power density. The system reduces reliance on rare-earth magnets and a China-centered electric actuator supply chain, aiming to improve automation ROI through higher payload, longer runtime, and lower cost in mid-payload (100\u2013500 kg) mobile robots.</p>\n<p>The company has progressed to a functioning integrated prototype (TRL 4) with &gt;$100k spent and is advancing toward a full-scale DHT and TRL 6 validation, with a roadmap focused on validating full-scale specs, signing pilots (LOI/MoU), and completing IP milestones (patent/FTO).</p>\n",
    "protected": false
   },
   "excerpt": {
    "rendered": "Digital hydraulic actuation for scalable mobile robots.",
    "protected": false
   },
