   "type": "company",
   "link": "https://hax.co/company/cargo-robotics/",
   "title": {
    "rendered": "Cargo Robotics"
   },
   "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>About Cargo Robotics: Founded by two Stanford grads who took delivery jobs at UPS and FedEx after a delivery mishap, Cargo Robotics is building a robotic delivery platform that brings advanced warehouse-style automation to delivery vans. Think of it like a warehouse on wheels. Our first product automates parcel loading and retrieval which saves 6+ hours of work per delivery vehicle every day. By fitting 30% more parcels in each vehicle, our technology also enables smaller warehouses and van fleets, and reduces injuries and delivery failures that cost carriers billions per year. This is the first step in our vision for a fully autonomous delivery system.</p>\n",
    "protected": false
   },
   "excerpt": {
    "rendered": "We\u2019re automating the last mile starting with robotic cargo bay for delivery vehicles.",
    "protected": false
   },
